   "gap": "Durrett PTE author version 5 of 11 January 2019, pp. 16-17 (PDF pp. 24-25), defines an extended random variable as a function whose domain is a set D in F and whose values lie in R* = [-inf, inf], measurable for the Borel sets of the usual topology on R* (generated by [-inf, a), (a, b), (b, inf]), and adopts X_inf = limsup X_n as the almost-sure limit defined on the whole space, possibly infinite. The handbook definition (measurable-probability.tex lines 302-321; line 237 says all functions are defined on all of the outcome space) excludes the domain-D variant, equips the extended line with the sigma-algebra generated by the rays [-inf, a] without proving that it equals the Borel sigma-algebra of the usual topology, and does not adopt or discuss the convention X_inf = limsup X_n.",
